    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 2927dcf3c16d8a69b707661552b8ca117de241f4 -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\n**What looks good**\n- `set_operation_coolant` runs the existing undoable `EditOperationParams::with_coolant` (`crates/app/src/mcp/coolant_tools.rs:76-89`), so it is one undo step and the same command the GUI picker runs. Validation is at command creation; unknown mode or operation is refused by name, with the valid words listed.\n- No `unwrap`/`expect`/panic in the new code. The warning-instead-of-refuse choice is recorded in `docs/decisions/954-mcp-op-coolant.md`; the post still refuses an unserved mode.\n- Placement is right: the new file reads the ECS world and a command, so it belongs in `app`. It has a provenance line, no new crate deps, and the new module keeps `tools.rs` (301 lines) and `job.rs` under the cap.\n- The tests cover the schema enum, undo/redo, refusals, warn/no-warn and the project round-trip.\n\n**Local results (trial-merged with current main, clean)**\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_coolant` | 5 passed |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp` | 19 passed |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean |\n\n**Requested before merge**\nNone.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- The camcraft-mcp skill row for `set_operation_coolant` (and `coolant` in `get_job`) still needs a process PR with a `PROCESS_VERSION` bump, as the body says. Please file the follow-up issue if it does not exist.\n- Body ends `Fixes #954`, has `Changelog:`; no `CHANGELOG.md` or snapshot changes.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
